# Swiping on past the last space fills a ring round a +, a tick each quarter; letting go with it
# full opens Create a Space, the new space going at the end (10 Nov 2026; SpaceCreateSwipe).
# 12 Nov 2026 (the owner's call): it takes a whole sidebar's width past the last space, so a casual
# swipe doesn't open it; it slides in as the page after the last space (CreateSpaceSlide) and the
# space gestures do nothing until Cancel or Create Space.
cra://debug?windowSize=1280x800
wait 2
# About half a sidebar past the last space (what used to fill the ring): nothing opens.
cra://debug?swipe=-14,12
wait 1
reject-log swipe past the last space opens Create a Space
# A long, deliberate swipe: it opens, sliding in.
cra://debug?swipe=-16,32
wait 1
expect-log swipe past the last space opens Create a Space
expect-log create a space slides: opening
expect-log create a space slid: card
cra://debug?windowState=creating
expect-log window state creating: main0 .*docked=1
# Open, a swipe doesn't page the spaces under it.
cra://debug?swipe=14,24
expect-log space swipe ignored: Create a Space is open
cra://debug?createSpace=cancel
expect-log create a space slides: cancelling
expect-log create a space slid: list
